      "problem": "$\\int (4\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+{sec}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C \\\\ \\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int (4\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+{sec}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 4\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+\\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4(-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
